Marius can load plugin packages written for other applications through an
independently implemented compatibility layer (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
That layer is a clean-room implementation written against publicly documented
behaviour. It contains no code from any other application, and loading a
third-party plugin does not change that plugin's own license, which its author
sets and which users must respect.

The application is named for Marius Michel Pasha (1819-1907), a French sailor
who, after being shipwrecked off the Ottoman coast, spent the rest of his life
building lighthouses along it.
